Hmm.. I might as well send you this list of earlier suggestions I've edited.
(Some new..)

Shopping mall
=============
Short of stuff? Running low on food? Visit your local shopping mall for
the best buys in dungeon! We have weapons, armor, food. Everything an
adventurer needs to survive. If you've got excess cash just deposit it
at our brand new Bank of Yendor. If you come during off-hours and find
the shops already closed, don't worry! Our slot machines supply you
all the essentials..

Wand of animation
=================
Try this new creation from the Magic Company of Yendor; the company that
brought you the famous wand of polymorph! This wand is GUARANTEED to 
brind life to statues and it is so powerfull that it will animate even
a food ration! Just imagine the face of that silly orc when you come with
a food ration trotting behind you! But beware of cursed animated weapons;
They might decide to hit the shopkeeper, on their own!

Parrot - a new pet
==================
"Squeeck! Polly wants a cracker!" Parrot is the pet for the modern
adventurer. Like the other pets we have to offer, a parrot can be trained
to carry things to you or help you in dire need. But being only a little
bird it can't carry very heavy items or do big harm to many monsters.
Nevertheless they have proved useful. Ever seen a black dragon who met
an angry parrot and lost both its eyes? Or perhaps you didn't know that
parrots just loooove to eat those killer bees and fortune cookies.
This excellent little animal also likes to sit on your shoulder and talk
all those nice things it just read in the fortune cookies..

Potion of oil
=============
This little addition to your supplies can recharge your worn out lamps.
Let there be more light! But beware. If you quaff one of these potions
it will make your hands slippery.. Also lighted potions of oil have been
known to go KABOOM!! after a little while, so be sure to throw them far
away from you.

Earplugs
========
Protect yourself from the roar of dragons and lions. Magical earplugs
also help you to hear monsters just around the corner, so you need not
be surprised.

Cage - a kind of box
====================
Beware this new devil's invention. Works like a box but holds monsters,
not objects. If you got yourself into one it would work just like a bear
trap but would be more difficult to get out of.. This item is also commonly
found in pet shops.

Minor changes
=============
Wands of polymorph are too powerful. They should have some chance of
disintegrating the object. On a pile of 5 objects this would be 0%. But
on a pile of 50 objects perhaps 50%. This would in effect make it 
impossible to collect large piles of junk, but still you could polymorph
small piles safely.

Door traps could be made more variant:
Bucket filled with water: can be put over a closed door and falls on the
			  one opening the door.
Falling door: when opened, falls over the player
Double door: when opened, reveals another door! (Once only, of course.)
(Revolving door: Can't be opened! When player tries this, the door only turns
		a whole turn! But.. When player can walk against it and finds
		himself on the other side.
		"Oops.. There was a monster on the other side. <more>"
		"You quickly return.")
Stuck lock: You break the key.
Various blade traps etc. Found from any AD&D or similar games in plenty.

Boxes can contain monsters. Easy to implement.. When you open a box
up springs the monster that was in it! It would be harder to let monsters
and YOU climb into the box, but more fun also. You would hide there..

Pets carry cursed things nowadays. Fix this! (Being related to corpses
they eat over those said cursed things.)

Monsters throw things at you unnaturally accurately, especially when you
are invisible. A BUG!

Perhaps some fishing gear you could use in all those pools..

Make it possible to empty potions and fill them from a fountain..

A rope to climb broken ladders and to tie sleeping monsters..

Uuh, seems like enough suggestions to last a pretty long time.. :-)
